{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, I'd make everyone able to *truly* feel what other people are feeling - even just for a few seconds.\n\nNot in a painful, overwhelming way, but just enough radical empathy that you couldn't ignore how your words and actions land on someone else.\n\nI think so many of our biggest problems come from disconnection. It's easy to be cruel, to be indifferent, to waste, to judge, or to hurt the planet when you don't viscerally feel the impact. If you *felt* what the lonely kid in your class feels, what a stranger on the other side of the world feels when they don't have clean water, or what future generations will feel living with our choices - you'd act differently without anyone having to force you.\n\nIf everyone had that, I don't think we'd need to legislate kindness or peace. People would naturally take care of each other, share more, listen more, waste less, and be a lot less afraid of people who seem different.\n\nIt would be like turning up the volume on our shared humanity.\n\nWhat about you? What would your one change be?",
